  r5-m08: refuted: duel state beats rival and its offline quartile predictions hold, but its stated mechanism (Code 3.0's longest MATH-500 problems driven to the 16,384 cap at T 1.0) is contradicted by the scored cell itself, which has 5 cap hits on 500 problems (base 27, Code 3.1 7), so the length-confined deficit it predicted comes from something other than cap hits.
  r5-m03: weak: duel state 'loses to rival' (-8.77, all 3 tests favour the rival's mixture account); its only offline gain rests on one test whose value fell outside its interval; and result-284db5 (top8 adds +8.5 on top of the cue, with RL-level Wait rates) contradicts its 'nothing more than the cue' core, although hard328 is formally outside its scope.
  r5-m10: refuted: duel state 'loses to rival' (-8.84 nats). In scope, on its own T3 file, plain answers that do not self-open but self-check later score +0.36 above other plain answers and come within 0.075 of cued answers on the same problems, which contradicts 'nothing after the opening adds'. Result-460e0a's 410 -> 372 drop under a fixed cue points the same way, and the part that survives (self-opened answers score like cued ones) is largely in Wang et al. App C.8.
